  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of length NNN, where each element is either a positive integer or the value −1-1−1.\n\nIt is guaranteed that A1≠−1A_1 \\neq -1A1​=−1.\n\nThere are NNN people, numbered from 111 to NNN.\n\n\nIf Ai≠−1A_i \\neq -1Ai​=−1, then person iii votes for the member numbered AiA_iAi​.\nIf Ai=−1A_i = -1Ai​=−1, then person iii looks at the prefix A1,A2,…,AiA_1, A_2, \\dots, A_iA1​,A2​,…,Ai​ in the array and considers only the positions j≤ij \\le ij≤i with Aj≠−1A_j \\neq -1Aj​=−1.\n\nLet freq(v)\\text{freq}(v)freq(v) be the number of times value vvv appears in this prefix.\n\nIf there is a **unique** value vvv with maximum freq(v)\\text{freq}(v)freq(v), then person iii votes for vvv.\nOtherwise, if two or more values share the maximum frequency, person iii does not vote.\n\n\nGiven a member XXX, determine whether there exists any valid rearrangement of the known values such that XXX receives the unique maximum number of votes (i.e., XXX wins without tying anyone else).\n\nNote that you may rearrange only the known values arbitrarily among their positions.\n\nPositions where Ai=−1A_i = -1Ai​=−1 must remain −1-1−1.\n\nPrint `Yes` if this is possible, and `No` otherwise.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input:\n\nThe first line contains an integer NNN and XXX — the length of the array and the member for whom we want to check if a winning arrangement is possible.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line `Yes` if member XXX can win for some rearrangement, otherwise `No`.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1001 \\leq A_i \\leq 1001≤Ai​≤100",
      "1≤X≤1001 \\le X \\le 1001≤X≤100",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 4⋅1054\\cdot 10^54⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
